        {
          "name": "rate",
          "required": true,
          "description": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Apply the pending-confirmation gate FIRST. After amount clarification, submit only a total already read back for this load and unambiguously affirmed by the caller. A reply containing a DIFFERENT complete amount is a correction even if it starts Yes: read back that new amount and wait for a fresh affirmative. No followed by the same digits is not confirmation. Yeah, 1125 after a clarification question also needs a readback and a later affirmative. Never negotiate while asking or waiting. With no pending clarification, ordinary clear asks/repeats and acceptance keep their direct behavior. Service-requested retries keep the same confirmed load and rate."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "after_final_offer",
          "description": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "Boolean flag. Use only the literal string true or false. For a new caller reply after this load's quoted final offer, use true. Otherwise use false. For a plain final refusal the TWO DIFFERENT fields are rate=decline and after_final_offer=true. Never put decline, money or words in this boolean field."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "description": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Send the caller's rate for one offered load, whether they accept our offer or counter. The service answers with a counter, a final offer, an agreement or a failure."
